<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
                  
                  
                <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\bm{p}}_{i}\}\leftarrow SS(\mathcal{I},{\mathbb{P}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\bm{p}}_{i}\}\leftarrow SS(\mathcal{I},{\mathbb{P}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
                  
                  
                <math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{\mathbf{Z}}}\leftarrow\textsc{SLat}(\{{\bm{p}}_{i}\},\mathcal{I},{\bm{P}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">SLat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{\mathbf{Z}}}\leftarrow\textsc{SLat}(\{{\bm{p}}_{i}\},\mathcal{I},{\bm{P}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
                  
                  
                <span id="alg3.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{GS}}({{\mathbf{Z}}}),{\mathcal{D}}_{\mathrm{mesh}}({{\mathbf{Z}}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>GS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>mesh</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{GS}}({{\mathbf{Z}}}),{\mathcal{D}}_{\mathrm{mesh}}({{\mathbf{Z}}}))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure></div></div>
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Image Patchification</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We precisely patchify an input image using point cloud coordinates extracted from the monocular depth estimator.
We can map a pixel <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{x,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{x,y}</annotation></semantics></math> to a coordinate of the point cloud <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{x,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{x,y}</annotation></semantics></math> in the extended latent space.
When <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{x,y}\in{\mathbb{W}}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{x,y}\in{\mathbb{W}}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, the 3D area corresponding to the given pixel is in the patch <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> since the structure was initialized with the depth estimator.
We therefore define the image patch <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{i,j}(\mathcal{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{i,j}(\mathcal{I})</annotation></semantics></math> by collecting all <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{x,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{x,y}</annotation></semantics></math> where corresponding <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{x,y}\in{\mathbb{W}}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{x,y}\in{\mathbb{W}}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, setting the other pixels to be black, and cropping out black regions so that the image becomes square.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Dilated Sampling</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We follow the recipe for dilated sampling in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>.
In this section, we assume that the unextended latent shape is <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\times K\times K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\times K\times K</annotation></semantics></math> for the sake of generalization. We divide the extended latent into <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\times K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\times K</annotation></semantics></math> non-overlapping patches so that the size of each patch is <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\times b\times K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\times b\times K</annotation></semantics></math>. We then randomly sample a pillar of 3D latent in each patch. The sampled pillars are attached by maintaining their relative positions to be a <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\times K\times K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\times K\times K</annotation></semantics></math> shaped latent. We sample <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\times b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\times b</annotation></semantics></math> samples without replacement, and we call them dilated samples. The dilated samples are passed through the pre-trained model with the image condition <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathcal{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> without image patchification. When dilated sampling is applied, <a href="#S4.E8" title="In 4.1 Overlapping Patch-wise Flow ‣ 4 Method ‣ Extend3D: Town-Scale 3D Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> is altered to be:</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E14X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{{{{\bm{v}}}}}({{\mathbf{Z}}}_{t},\mathcal{I},t)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{{{{\bm{v}}}}}({{\mathbf{Z}}}_{t},\mathcal{I},t)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1-\gamma_{t})\mathrm{PatchWise}({{\mathbf{Z}}}_{t},C_{\mathcal{I}},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>PatchWise</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1-\gamma_{t})\mathrm{PatchWise}({{\mathbf{Z}}}_{t},C_{\mathcal{I}},t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E14Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\gamma_{t}\mathrm{Dilated}({{\mathbf{Z}}}_{t},C_{\mathcal{I}},t)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Dilated</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\gamma_{t}\mathrm{Dilated}({{\mathbf{Z}}}_{t},C_{\mathcal{I}},t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{t}=0.5\cos^{\alpha}(\pi-\pi t)+0.5," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{t}=0.5\cos^{\alpha}(\pi-\pi t)+0.5,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PatchWise}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>PatchWise</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PatchWise}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to <a href="#S4.E8" title="In 4.1 Overlapping Patch-wise Flow ‣ 4 Method ‣ Extend3D: Town-Scale 3D Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is a hyperparameter. We set <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=5</annotation></semantics></math> in our experiments. We use dilated sampling only for sparse structure generation because we empirically observed that it worsens texture when applied to structured latent generation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Computational Cost</h3>

<figure id="A1.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 7</span>: </span><span id="A1.T7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Computational costs of 3D generation methods.<span id="A1.T7.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> 
<br class="ltx_break">(<math id="A1.T7.m2" class="ltx_centering" alttext="a=b=2,d=4,n_{\mathrm{iter}}=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>iter</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=b=2,d=4,n_{\mathrm{iter}}=5</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></figcaption>
<div id="A1.T7.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:347.8pt;height:82.4pt;vertical-align:-38.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(18.4pt,-4.4pt) scale(1.11848103181442,1.11848103181442) ;">
<table id="A1.T7.6.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T7.6.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"></td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt">VRAM (GB)</td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Time (min)</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.6.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Trellis <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite></td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">17</td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.06</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.6.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">Hunyuan3D <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>]</cite></td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">56</td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.78</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.6.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">SynCity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite></td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">49</td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">52.0</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.6.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">EvoScene <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">48</a>]</cite></td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">68</td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">35.3</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.6.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r"><span id="A1.T7.6.1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ours</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r"><span id="A1.T7.6.1.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">28</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.6.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A1.T7.6.1.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">14.1</span></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compared the computational cost of our method with previous methods in <a href="#A1.T7" title="In A.4 Computational Cost ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Extend3D: Town-Scale 3D Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, using an NVIDIA RTX Pro 6000. Although our pipeline is heavier than object-centric methods (Trellis or Hunyuan3D), it requires substantially less memory and time than other scene-level pipelines.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Memory cost.</span>
For <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=b=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=b=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=4</annotation></semantics></math> case, the peak GPU memory used for our method is 28GB. Most of the memory is utilized in <span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SLat</span> optimization process. Without <span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SLat</span> optimization, it took 14GB VRAM. Also, for <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=b=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=b=6</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=4</annotation></semantics></math>, without the <span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SLat</span> optimization, the peak memory was 61 GB. <a href="#S5.T2" title="In 5.2 Quantitative Results ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Extend3D: Town-Scale 3D Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows that our Extend3D achieves promising results even without <span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SLat</span> optimization. Therefore, we can ensure reasonable quality with limited GPU resources.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inference time.</span> The computational complexity of our method is <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(abd^{2}n_{\mathrm{iter}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>iter</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(abd^{2}n_{\mathrm{iter}})</annotation></semantics></math>. A larger (larger <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>), better detailed (larger <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>), and more complete (larger <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{iter}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>iter</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{iter}}</annotation></semantics></math>) scene requires more inference time, so there is a trade-off between output quality and inference time.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Rigorous Definition</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, we provide a detailed and rigorous definition of <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i,j}^{\mathrm{SS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>SS</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i,j}^{\mathrm{SS}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i,j}^{\mathrm{\textsc{SLat}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">SLat</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i,j}^{\mathrm{\textsc{SLat}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi_{i,j}^{\mathrm{SS}})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>SS</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi_{i,j}^{\mathrm{SS}})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi_{i,j}^{\mathrm{\textsc{SLat}}})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">SLat</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi_{i,j}^{\mathrm{\textsc{SLat}}})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for clarity. Firstly, we define patchification <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> through sliding windows as:</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{W}}_{i,j}^{K}=\left[\frac{iK}{d},\frac{iK}{d}+K\right)\times\left[\frac{jK}{d},\frac{jK}{d}+K\right)\times[K]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝕎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{W}}_{i,j}^{K}=\left[\frac{iK}{d},\frac{iK}{d}+K\right)\times\left[\frac{jK}{d},\frac{jK}{d}+K\right)\times[K],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i,j}^{\mathrm{SS}}({{\mathbf{Z}}}_{t}^{\mathrm{SS}})=({{\mathbf{Z}}}_{t}^{\mathrm{SS}})_{{\mathbb{W}}_{i,j}^{N}}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times N\times N}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>SS</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>SS</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>SS</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>𝕎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i,j}^{\mathrm{SS}}({{\mathbf{Z}}}_{t}^{\mathrm{SS}})=({{\mathbf{Z}}}_{t}^{\mathrm{SS}})_{{\mathbb{W}}_{i,j}^{N}}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times N\times N},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\phi_{i,j}^{\mathrm{\textsc{SLat}}}\!\left({{\mathbf{Z}}}_{t}^{\mathrm{\textsc{SLat}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">SLat</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">SLat</mtext></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phi_{i,j}^{\mathrm{\textsc{SLat}}}\!\left({{\mathbf{Z}}}_{t}^{\mathrm{\textsc{SLat}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Biggl\{\Bigl({\bm{p}}-\Bigl(\tfrac{iM}{d},\,\tfrac{jM}{d},\,0\Bigr),{{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}\Bigr):" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>−</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.278em">)</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Biggl\{\Bigl({\bm{p}}-\Bigl(\tfrac{iM}{d},\,\tfrac{jM}{d},\,0\Bigr),{{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}\Bigr):</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E18Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle({\bm{p}},{{\mathbf{z}}}_{t})\in{{\mathbf{Z}}}_{t}^{\mathrm{\textsc{SLat}}},\;{\bm{p}}\in{\mathbb{W}}_{i,j}^{M}\Biggr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">SLat</mtext></msup><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕎</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle({\bm{p}},{{\mathbf{z}}}_{t})\in{{\mathbf{Z}}}_{t}^{\mathrm{\textsc{SLat}}},\;{\bm{p}}\in{\mathbb{W}}_{i,j}^{M}\Biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The subtraction in <a href="#A1.E18" title="In A.5 Rigorous Definition ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Extend3D: Town-Scale 3D Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> is for coordinate normalization into <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[M]^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[M]^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Secondly, the inversions of these processes are defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi_{i,j}^{\mathrm{SS}})^{-1}({\bm{X}})_{x,y,z}=\mathbf{1}_{(x,y,z)\in{\mathbb{W}}^{N}_{i,j}}\cdot{\bm{X}}_{x-\frac{iN}{d},y-\frac{jN}{d},z}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>SS</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi_{i,j}^{\mathrm{SS}})^{-1}({\bm{X}})_{x,y,z}=\mathbf{1}_{(x,y,z)\in{\mathbb{W}}^{N}_{i,j}}\cdot{\bm{X}}_{x-\frac{iN}{d},y-\frac{jN}{d},z},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E20X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\phi_{i,j}^{\mathrm{\textsc{SLat}}})^{-1}({\bm{X}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">SLat</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\phi_{i,j}^{\mathrm{\textsc{SLat}}})^{-1}({\bm{X}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Biggl({\bm{X}}+\Bigl(\Bigl(\tfrac{iM}{d},\,\tfrac{jM}{d},\,0\Bigr),\bm{0}\Bigr)\Biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo mathsize="2.600em">,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo mathsize="2.600em">,</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Biggl({\bm{X}}+\Bigl(\Bigl(\tfrac{iM}{d},\,\tfrac{jM}{d},\,0\Bigr),\bm{0}\Bigr)\Biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E20Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cup\;\Bigl\{({\bm{p}},\bm{0}):{\bm{p}}\in\{{\bm{p}}_{i}\},\;\forall{{\mathbf{z}}}~({\bm{p}},{{\mathbf{z}}})\notin{\bm{X}}\Bigr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">∪</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∉</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cup\;\Bigl\{({\bm{p}},\bm{0}):{\bm{p}}\in\{{\bm{p}}_{i}\},\;\forall{{\mathbf{z}}}~({\bm{p}},{{\mathbf{z}}})\notin{\bm{X}}\Bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">setting the value of other positions to zero.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Ablation on Iterative SDEdit</h3>

<figure id="A1.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 8</span>: </span><span id="A1.T8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation study on varying number of iterations <math id="A1.T8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{iter}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>iter</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{iter}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
